    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0223" n="117" xml:id="pg117"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./79: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-07-10T18:00:00-04:00">July 10, 1934—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>152. Your 177 and 178, July 9. Our attitude on London naval conversations and
                    conference is expressed in our 141, June 27.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d124-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Department has made no announcement, official or unofficial, relative to matter
                    of bilateral, non-aggressive pact with Soviet Union.</p>
                <p>Your statement minimizes hope of effective negotiations with Troyanovsky, but if
                    and when he offers to negotiate, we will canvass entire situation with him and
                    endeavor to impress him with the importance of speedy agreement as alternative
                    to dissolving bank and foregoing expectation of better trade relations based
                    upon assistance by our Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
